  "description": "Parsnips are one of my favorite root vegetables. They're intensely sweet and earthy, but on their own they can be a little bland. The key to turning them into a creamy soup with a clean, pure flavor is to reach for some unexpected aromatics that both complement and contrast, like jalapeño, ginger, and coriander seed.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Whipped cream lightly flavored with ground allspice, for garnish; Cayenne pepper, for garnish\n\nOptional substitutions: low-sodium chicken stock → vegetable stock",
